First Author: Dag
Title: A data-guided analytical framework for assessing the value of additional variables in heart transplant decision making
Source number: 61

Very short summary: This retrospective national-registry study analysed 25,512 UNOS heart transplant cases from the post-2004 era and assessed whether variables added to the registry in 2004 improved 1-month, 1-year, and 5-year graft-survival prediction. Five classification algorithms were evaluated using five-fold cross-validation with nested feature selection and class-imbalance handling; SVM produced the best balanced 1-year performance (AUC 0.6342), but the additional variables did not meaningfully improve discrimination.

