	•	Hyperparameter Tuning Reported: Not Reported
	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The authors compared Tree-Augmented Naïve Bayes, logistic regression, SVM, decision tree, and random forest models using five-fold cross-validation. SVM models were reported to outperform the other algorithms across the three time horizons; the selected balanced 1-year model was SVM_RUS using 33 old variables. Automated feature selection combined information-gain fast feature selection, LASSO, and Cox regression, supplemented by predictors identified from the literature. Feature selection was repeated within each training fold to reduce leakage. Interpretability was addressed through normalized sensitivity analysis, ranked variable-importance plots, and a TAN-derived directed acyclic graph. No explicit hyperparameter-tuning procedure was reported.

