	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Missing numerical values were imputed using the median, while missing categorical observations were assigned an “UNKNOWN” category. Invariant variables, outliers, identifiers, and variables considered unrelated to survival were checked and removed. Class imbalance was addressed using random under-sampling and cost-sensitive models; RUS was applied only to each training fold, leaving the corresponding test fold at its natural class distribution. Exact per-fold training and test counts were not reported, and neither source code nor trained model weights were reported.

